# Supabase configuration for the CVKM HSS admin backend.
#
# This file lists variable NAMES only — no real values. Copy it to .env.local
# and fill in the real values once a dedicated CVKM Supabase project exists.
# Never commit .env.local (or any file with real secrets) to git.

# Project URL and publishable (browser-safe) API key, from
# Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables are bundled into client-side JavaScript by
# Next.js, so only ever put values here that are safe for a visitor's
# browser to see.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# Also called the "anon key" in older Supabase projects/dashboards.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Service role (secret) key. Grants full access to the database, bypassing
# Row Level Security entirely.
#
# MUST stay server-only:
#   - never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_
#   - never import into a Client Component
#   - never send in a response body, header, or client-visible payload
#   - never commit to git
#
# Used only by trusted server-side code (e.g. the first-super_admin
# bootstrap procedure, or a future admin invitation flow) that must call
# the Supabase Auth admin API. Most admin operations should NOT need this
# key — they should authenticate as the signed-in user and rely on RLS.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
